-- title:
--   Two-branch normalisation at a node, with node order -m
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q \ge 5$, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ with decidable equality, and let $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$ be a ring homomorphism whose zero set is exactly the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $a \in k$ satisfy $a \in$ `ssJSet q k`, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$ with $j$-invariant $a$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$, together with $a^{q^2} = a$, $a \ne 0$ and $a \ne 1728$. Let $f \ne 0$ lie in `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the full level-$q$ modular function field inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q^{1/1}))$-style Laurent series, and assume that $\operatorname{ord}_W f = 0$ for every place $W$ of this field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ that is centred at the node $(a, a^q)$, in the sense that some $x \in A$ with $\mathrm{red}\,x = a$ has $\operatorname{ord}_W(j_q - x) > 0$ and some $y \in A$ with $\mathrm{red}\,y = a^q$ has $\operatorname{ord}_W(j_q \circ (q\text{-expansion}) - y) > 0$, where $\operatorname{ord}_W$ is minus the logarithm of the associated adic valuation. Then there are $c \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $c \ne 0$ and $m \in \mathbb{Z}$ such that: the Laurent series underlying $c \cdot f$ lies in `CharPReduction.modularLocalized (1 * q) A.toSubring red`, the localisation of the modular ring of level $q$ at the prime kernel of coefficientwise reduction; the Laurent series underlying `frickeInvolutionBar (1 * q)` applied to $(c q^m) \cdot f$ lies in the same subring; the reduction of $c \cdot f$ under `CharPReduction.modularRedLocHom` lies in `modularFunctionFieldC k 1`, the subfield of $k$-Laurent series generated by `jqModC k` and `jqNModC k 1`; both this reduction and the reduction of the Fricke transform of $(c q^m) \cdot f$ are nonzero; and the first component of `frobNodePair q a`, namely the place `charLGeomPlaceOfPoint k a`, assigns to the reduction of $c \cdot f$, viewed in `modularFunctionFieldC k 1`, the order $-m$.
--
--   This is the two-branch normalisation of a function on $X_0(q)$ at a width-one supersingular crossing, in the local picture $xy = q$ of Deligne–Rapoport, strengthened by the identification of the Gauss jump $m$ across the node with minus the order of vanishing of the near-branch reduction at the place $\bar j = a$. It feeds the slope-law statements for the annuli and charts around such a node.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_NodeLocalized_exists_twoBranchNormalisation_qpow_and_ord_charLGeomPlaceOfPoint_eq_neg.lean

